/* book: the chapter, paragraph by paragraph (first sentences):
   - Normalize the load first. z = Z/Z0 = r + jx.
   - The reflection coefficient is Γ = (Z − Z0)/(Z + Z0) = (z − 1)/(z + 1). Γ is complex: Γ = Γr + jΓi.
   - Special points fix the chart.
   - r and x are normalized resistance and reactance; centres and radii are in the Γ plane.
   - Constant-r circles touch the right point Γ = +1.
   - Every point at the same radius has the same |Γ|.
   - ΓL is the load reflection coefficient; d is the distance from the load toward the generator in metres; β = 2π/λ is the phase constant in rad/m; λ is the guide wavelength in metres.
   - The exponent changes phase by 2βd.
   - Admittance uses the same chart. y = Y/Y0 = 1/z = g + jb.
   - Shunt stubs are easier on the admittance side.
*/
