/* book exam traps: Using εr instead of εeff in λg and vp; the wave sees air plus dielectric, so it travels faster than a wave in bulk dielectric. | Calling microstrip pure TEM. It is quasi-TEM and has dispersion; stripline in a homogeneous dielectric is the pure-TEM printed line. | Mixing up microstrip and stripline: microstrip has air above the strip; stripline has the strip buried between two ground planes. | Putting W and h into a ratio formula with different units, or treating W/h as if it had units. Only the dimensionless ratio enters. | Ignoring skin effect, dielectric loss and radiation loss at high frequency; conductor loss rises roughly as √f and radiation grows on thick, low-εr substrates. */
